# Configuration file for the 'beep' utility on Red Hat-based systems.
# This file controls how the pcspkr (PC Speaker) kernel module is handled.
#
# NOTE: The pcspkr.ko driver is part of kernel-modules-extra and is
# not installed by default. Loading it may require manual intervention
# or specific kernel module dependencies that are difficult to automate
# cleanly via package managers due to potential side-effects (e.g.
# installing -debug kernel packages).
#
# In containerized environments, access to the actual hardware PC speaker
# is often restricted or unavailable. The behavior of the 'beep' command
# here may vary depending on the host's capabilities and container configuration.

{% raw %}
# Uncomment the alias line below to automatically load the pcspkr kernel
# module when the beep service or script requires it.
{% endraw %}

# The alias command to load the pcspkr kernel module.
# Schema description: The alias command to load the pcspkr kernel module. Commented out by default.
# Format: alias <alias_name> <module_name>
# Default: '# alias platform:pcspkr pcspkr'
{{ alias_pcspkr | default('# alias platform:pcspkr pcspkr') }}
